**Proposition 5.3 (route agreement and dynamics).** All current
Boundary/Space-orbit/numerical-Memory conversions agree and commute
with every defined native call on their current images. Time-to-current
conversion agrees with both the actual scan and retained simulation.
There is no claimed arbitrary-current-to-measured-past inverse.

Proof. Each current decoder returns the same $(A,w)/G_K$. For a
complete call $a$, Theorem 3.1 makes the successor $U_a$ and whole
output well defined on these orbits, including growth's changed
geometry. Write $e_i,d_i$ for each current encoding/decoder and
$e_i',d_i'$ for the corresponding successor encoding/decoder, in
the actual successor context. On their respective images both
composites are identities. Therefore

$$
 (e_j'd_i')(e_i'U_ad_i)=e_j'U_ad_i
   =(e_j'U_ad_j)(e_jd_i),
 \qquad (e_hd_j)(e_jd_i)=e_hd_i.
\tag{SC.14}
$$

These identities compare numerical conversions of one actual
successor, with its actual new context and paid exports. Proper
pending prefixes carry their actual parser state and no completed
field update, as already checked in the interface induction. A fresh
measured Time record requires the real calls and returned scalars;
computed germ updates do not create one. At startup every route uses
the same (SC.10), so the source execution, Time decoder and predictor
simulation agree. For later arbitrary calls, append their actual
records if a temporal record is desired and advance the predictor;
no erasure of the journal is declared reversible. $\square$

